*2 [[Sir Seal]]s spawn after 153.33 seconds<sup>4,600f</sup>, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage is difficult without the right cats, and given the boss' Omni Strike reaching most of the viable midrangers, you'll need to make it your goal to minimize its impact by any means necessary. [[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Macho Crystal Cat]] and [[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Tourist Cat]] are absolutely necessary for any strategy using [[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Jagando Jr.]], as they will keep him safe from the Jumbo Fireworks Craftsmen's high pierce. [[Driller Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Neo Driller Cat]] is one of the only units that can completely hold them in place for extended periods of time, meaning that outranging them is not a consistent strategy without it. If you're not using Driller Cat, treat the boss as you would St. Dober, and use your units gradually wear them down while preventing them from attacking as much as possible. [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk]] can help fill in the gaps and keep enemies slowed.

Late game players can use [[Dogumaru (Special Cat)|Reborn Warrior Doguemon]] and [[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Hitman Cat]] for consistent chip damage regardless of your strategy, while endgame players can reliably outrange it with [[Talents|Talented]] [[Filibuster Cat X (Special Cat)|Metafilibuster]] or [[Master of Logic Newtone (Special Cat)|Newtone]].

